{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1075307-ghost-summoning-and-anchors","id":1075307,"title":"Ghost Summoning and Anchors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-08T17:10:03-07:00","id":1075307,"title":"Ghost Summoning and Anchors","content":"I was just rereading &quot;Ghost Summoning&quot; and realized it says that even under the power the of the summons &quot;The ghost cannot travel farther than allowed by<br /> its Anchor.&quot;<br /> This confuses me for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1.) For most ghosts outside the underworld, the anchor gives a range of 10 or 20 feet. Why bother with the summons? Just use &quot;speak to the dead&quot; and you can see the poor thing across the room, then give it a command with death 2 if you like. I guess some ghosts may have an entire house as an anchor, but it still seems it would be easier to stroll through the house and look.<br /> <br /> 2.) It was my understanding that Anchors don't allow or not allow a ghost to move any given distance, they only prevent essence bleed within its small area, so why would this be a restriction at all?<br /> <br /> Am I confused about something (heaven knows I have been before)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T18:02:15-07:00","id":1075314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1075307-ghost-summoning-and-anchors#post1075307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.) It was my understanding that Anchors don't allow or not allow a ghost to move any given distance, they only prevent essence bleed within its small area, so why would this be a restriction at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>If we discount the possibility that this is an artifact that missed the errata pass, it's worth pointing out that the two caster-side range limitations of the spell are &quot;nearest nonspecific target within sensory range&quot; and &quot;specific target from anywhere.&quot; A summons from three counties away is not going to give a homebound specter the resources to make that journey on their natural Essence stores.<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that Ghost Summons is a spell that leans heavily on its Reach effects; you can call a ghost to you and compel it to manifest and/or do things for you with a single spell instead of having to sustain two separate effects to keep it on task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T04:26:55-07:00","id":1075431,"title":"","content":"I don't think that it should possible to summon anything from across the globe. Without the sympathy you are limited to your scale factor.<br /> <br /> About the Ghosts... Just add Reach to allow for leaving anchor. It's acting counter their interest but still doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:11:07-07:00","id":1075463,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses. It does make a bit more sense in context now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:46:34-07:00","id":1075476,"title":"","content":"Something worth noting: Ghosts don't have to stay by their Anchors anymore. That was a thing in 1e. Now, Anchors just prevent essence bleed when they're within its range. A ghost actually <i>can</i> leave that radius. They likewise can no longer hop instantly from Anchor to Anchor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T21:10:53-07:00","id":1075712,"title":"","content":"So I will throw a similar question I have in this thread. Is there any limits on what an Anchor can be? Could an ephemeral being anchor to say an entire house?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T21:58:31-07:00","id":1075731,"title":"","content":"No limits to my knowledge. A house is a fine Anchor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 04-10-2017, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:31:12-07:00","id":1075906,"title":"","content":"There was a nice thread somewhere in the general forum that talked a lot about Anchors and how they changed in 2nd ED, including why Anchors that are things like emotions are a good awesome thing to use in your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T03:11:50-07:00","id":1077609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1075307-ghost-summoning-and-anchors?p=1075906#post1075906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a nice thread somewhere in the general forum that talked a lot about Anchors and how they changed in 2nd ED, including why Anchors that are things like emotions are a good awesome thing to use in your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>would be useful, I'm planning to roll a Moros necromancer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}